      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Desert",
            "Hills",
            "Plains",
            "Seasonal grasslands of Zakhara"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A slender pale-amber flying insect about 2 inches long, with a straw-like body and nearly transparent wings."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Special attacks mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Bite · Deals 1 damage. A human or non-burden animal saves vs. paralyzation or develops sore, swollen joints. The separate beast-of-burden rule causes back pain and weakness that prevents carrying loads or traveling far.",
            "Recovery · A cure disease spell cures the effect. Without magical treatment it lasts about two weeks."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Traits mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Fragile · Any hit destroys an individual. Normal or magical cold and fire can harm it. It drowns if submerged and prevented from getting out."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Encounters mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Arrival at Adhal · The affected camels show symptoms on the second night of travel. A successful Desert Survival or Healing proficiency check identifies the cause. See Adventure Book p. 8."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "Neutral, animal intelligence 1, morale 6. Uncommon, daytime, omnivorous, and encountered in groups of 6–60. The block gives each insect 1 HP.",
            "The source gives a paralyzation save for people and other animals and gives no separate save in the beast-of-burden paragraph.",
            "The second-night timing belongs to the camel encounter. The animal entry gives no general onset time.",
            "TSR, Corsairs of the Great Sea (1994), unnumbered Monstrous Compendium leaf, p. 100."
          ]
        }
      ],
